# Version branches

Each supported Minecraft / mod-loader version has its own git branch that acts as **that version's main**. Do not treat a single default branch as the only source of truth. Game version (and loader) determine which branch to inspect, reproduce on, and fix in.

## Currently published / supported

| Minecraft | Loader | Branch |
|-----------|--------|--------|
| 1.20.1 | Forge | `forge-1.20.1` (repo default) |
| 1.21.1 | NeoForge | `neoforge-1.21.1` |

Bugs, features, and PRs for a supported version belong on that version's branch.

## Other branches

Older or experimental branches exist from port attempts that are **not published** or **no longer supported** (one-person project, limited time). Examples include `forge-1.19.x`, `neoforge-1.20.6`, `neoforge-1.21.3`, `1.17.1`, `1.16`, and `1.15.2-for-forge-31.2.45`.

- Do not assume these versions are supported unless the user explicitly says so.
- Do not spend significant time porting or fixing unpublished/unsupported versions unless asked.
- If a bug is reported for an unsupported game version, say so and point the reporter at a supported version when appropriate.

## When investigating a bug

1. Read the reported Minecraft version, loader, and loader version.
2. Map that to the matching version branch above (or report that the version is unsupported).
3. Work on that branch. Do not mix fixes across version branches unless the same change is being backported/forward-ported on purpose.
